		<IComment type="e">
			<_id type="a">GUID 0ed27525-5053-4475-b210-a62fa7eeb3ee</_id>
			<_myState type="a">10240</_myState>
			<_name type="a">comment_93</_name>
			<_modifiedTimeWeak type="a">2.18.2026::6:54:49</_modifiedTimeWeak>
			<_description type="p"><IDescription type="e">
				<_textRTF type="a">{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\deflang1033{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset0 Arial;}}%0D
\viewkind4\uc1\pard\ulwave\fs20 Tx\ulnone  path(write): before I2C write, build CRC over device address/register/data and append to buffer in PmicCdd_I2CASynctransmit/PmicCddI2CSyncTransmit\par%0D
\par%0D
Rx path (read) : set RxLength = 2(data +CRC) when CRC enabled, then compute and compare in PmicCddI2CSyncTransmit/PmicCddI2cEndNotification\par%0D
}%0D
</_textRTF>
			</IDescription>
			</_description>
			<_modifiedTime type="a">2.18.2026::6:5:45</_modifiedTime>
		</IComment>
		<IComment type="e">
			<_id type="a">GUID f6d25db1-9256-4753-bdb5-2b1c37e4bdf5</_id>
			<_myState type="a">10240</_myState>
			<_name type="a">comment_94</_name>
			<_modifiedTimeWeak type="a">2.18.2026::6:54:49</_modifiedTimeWeak>
			<_description type="p"><IDescription type="e">
				<_text type="a">I2CAsyncTransmit%0D
Callback</_text>
			</IDescription>
			</_description>
			<_modifiedTime type="a">2.18.2026::6:5:45</_modifiedTime>
		</IComment>
		<IConstraint type="e">
			<_id type="a">GUID 89f3b4b6-b49b-44b3-b055-096c9a48974c</_id>
			<_myState type="a">8192</_myState>
			<_name type="a">SM_InternalVoltageMonitoring</_name>
			<_modifiedTimeWeak type="a">2.18.2026::6:54:49</_modifiedTimeWeak>
			<_description type="p"><IDescription type="e">
				<_text type="a">s1. The CONFIG2 register should be passed as the 1st sequence during the PMICCDD Initialization.%0D
%0D
2. Whenever the fault is injected , both nINT and RESET pin are pulled low hwere the PMIC itself taking the safety action%0D
%0D
3. The BUCKx_VOUT and LDOx_VOUT registers should not be programmed by in the VIP software and should npt be changed during runtime.%0D
%0D
4. The Under volatge testing and Vcca testing is ot performed as HW team instructed not to do which may cause the board damage %0D
%0D
5. nINT TOP register is read after the CRC sequence and before all the PMIC initialiation sequence to get the interrupt set information%0D
%0D
6. During UV/OV Fault , PMIC is performing reset before notifying to the HOST via Int pin. Hence reset reason read perform after RESET. %0D
Clarification Ticket is raised on TI &amp; details are mentioned below:- %0D
E2E ticket - https://e2e.ti.com/e2eprivate/visteon/visteon-infotainment/f/visteon-infotainment-forum/1446887/tps65224-q1-pmiccdd-under-voltage-and-over-voltage-testing?pifragment-322104=1#5888374</_text>
			</IDescription>
			</_description>
			<_modifiedTime type="a">2.18.2026::6:6:25</_modifiedTime>
		</IConstraint>
		<IComment type="e">
			<_id type="a">GUID 33fe97b1-5e54-48a9-bc43-b15fccbf50a3</_id>
			<_myState type="a">10240</_myState>
